WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.799
The home of architects, Dorota and Mariusz
Szlachcic is right on Kleciński Park on the

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.390
outskirts of the Polish city of Wroclaw.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.100
„Hello, welcome in our house.”

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.170
The tour starts upstairs.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.320
Only the garage and utility rooms are at ground
level.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:25.390
The home's 200 square meters of living space
has been divided up according to a clear principle.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.520
“Our house is a part of nature and is built
in Kleciński Park.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:40.500
We divided it into three zones: Utility zone,
day zone and night zone,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.560
with bedroom and bathroom.”

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.390
The heart of the day area is a large living
space inspired by Japanese architecture.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.700
The couple has been to Japan several times.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:59.860
The dining room and open-plan kitchen are
also located on the first floor.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.960
The adjacent terrace is conveniently located
for dining out of doors.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.980
"This terrace is 
connected with the dining room.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:21.460
This table was designed by us to move to the
terrace.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.430
We can eat, dining with our friends.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:30.100
We are inside, but outside.”

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.760
The exterior is clad in copper and wood to
blend in with the natural surroundings.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.920
The couple have been living in their dream
house since 2014.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.409
At that time, all three children had moved
out and the two architects were able to make

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:56.280
their ideas a reality in natural surroundings
on a narrow piece of land.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:06.560
Despite all the openness, there are elements
that create private spaces -- the central,

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.450
concrete stairway, for example.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:19.120
“The idea of this house was to have a very,
very small house connected with the nature,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:26.739
but with an element, which guards our privacy.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.380
It's this staircase.”

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:34.239
The stairway goes up right through the middle
of the house and takes us into the house's

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:35.450
nighttime area.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.500
It's mainly open plan here as well.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.780
“When we are having a bath, we can look
at the park.”

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.600
Yet the residents are still screened from
prying eyes.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:03:02.800
„When we are here, we are looking at trees
and the sky and all is perfect.”

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:14.420
In addition to the bedroom and bathroom, the
upper floor also has a guest room and large wardrobe .

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.920
The openness of the design and the views outside
make the house seem bigger than it really is.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.500
The natrual setting makes the house particularly
beautiful in summer.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.420
But what's the atmosphere like during other
seasons?

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:42.799
“We love winter, when the surrounding is
very white and it is a part of our house too,

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.160
because our house is white inside too.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:56.380
When we have fall, all is red and yellow.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.800
And it looks amazing.”

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.879
No matter what season,

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:07.080
the architects enjoy their open, yet very
private house set in leafy, green surroundings.

